<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <PackageId>HttpResilience.NET</PackageId>
    <Version>3.0.0</Version>
    <Authors>BAPS Dev Team</Authors>
    <Description>Standardised HTTP client resilience for .NET services: a validated configuration schema, safe defaults (unsafe HTTP methods are never retried or hedged), connection-pool standardisation and bounded telemetry, over Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience and Polly.</Description>
    <PackageTags>http;resilience;polly;httpclient;retry;circuit-breaker</PackageTags>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/baps-apps/http-resilience-net/</PackageProjectUrl>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) BAPS. All rights reserved.</Copyright>
    <!-- Proprietary: the terms ship as a file because no SPDX expression applies. -->
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>3.0.0 has breaking changes. These nine change behavior without a compile error:
1. Enabled now defaults to true: every client registered with AddHttpResilienceHandler or AddHttpResilienceHedgingHandler gets the pipeline unless its section says Enabled: false. HttpResilience:Enabled: false at the root turns every client off.
2. Telemetry names moved out of OpenTelemetry's reserved http.* namespace: instruments are http_resilience.circuit_breaker.state, http_resilience.limiter.available_permits and http_resilience.limiter.queued_requests; tags are http_resilience.client.name, http_resilience.authority and http_resilience.limiter.kind. The breaker gauge now has one series per state (tag http_resilience.circuit_breaker.state = closed, open or half_open; 1 for the current state) and reports every breaker from startup. Update dashboards and alerts.
3. Log categories are HttpResilience.NET.Configuration, HttpResilience.NET.Pipeline and HttpResilience.NET.Limiter instead of HttpResilience. Update Logging:LogLevel entries and log queries.
4. A hedged client refuses an unlisted authority with InvalidOperationException, not HttpRequestException, so retry policies no longer repeat it as transient. A catch (HttpRequestException) that relied on catching it must catch InvalidOperationException.
5. Retry waits are capped by the new Retry:MaxDelay (default 5 seconds). A Retry-After longer than it ends the retries and returns the 429 or 503 at once, instead of waiting until Timeout:Total. Raise Retry:MaxDelay for a dependency that asks for longer waits.
6. Resilience handlers registered on a client before AddHttpResilienceHandler are replaced (event 17), so .NET Aspire ServiceDefaults need no RemoveAllResilienceHandlers() call. A resilience handler registered on the client itself before AddHttpResilienceHandler fails client creation: move AddResilienceHandler after it. A disabled client loses the ConfigureHttpClientDefaults resilience handlers too (event 19), so the kill switch never falls back to a pipeline that retries POST.
7. Circuit breaker defaults are CircuitBreaker:MinimumThroughput 20 (was 100) and FailureRatio 0.5 (was 0.1): a breaker now opens on low-traffic clients where it never did. Check alerts on http_resilience.circuit_breaker.state and handling of BrokenCircuitException; set 100 and 0.1 at the root to keep the old behavior.
8. Code that changes a client's platform resilience options after this package wrote them (AddStandardResilienceHandler(configure), Configure, PostConfigure or ConfigureAll of HttpStandardResilienceOptions or HttpStandardHedgingResilienceOptions, a second AddStandardHedgingHandler) fails client creation, naming each changed property. Move such values to the client's section or AddHttpResilienceHandler(configure).
9. With Connection:Enabled, a finite SetHandlerLifetime, a configured HttpClientHandler, or a supplied SocketsHttpHandler whose connect or pool settings differ from the configured ones fails client creation instead of being silently replaced or overwritten.
Also: an unknown configuration key fails startup; ConcurrencyLimiter:Backstop above 10,000 fails startup; a Polly v7 handler on a configured client logs Warning event 20; Polly dependencies are capped below 9.0.0.
Compile errors with obvious replacements: per-client registration is AddHttpResilienceHandler() / AddHttpResilienceHedgingHandler(); every public type is in HttpResilience.NET and starts with HttpResilience (RetryOptions is HttpResilienceRetryOptions); the health check and ValidateHttpResilienceClientsOnStart() are removed; RetryableMethods and Authorities are read-only lists.
Full list: https://github.com/baps-apps/http-resilience-net/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>

    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
    <!-- The last published version, even across a major: every break from it is either a reviewed entry in
         CompatibilitySuppressions.xml or a pack failure. -->
    <PackageValidationBaselineVersion>2.0.0</PackageValidationBaselineVersion>
    <!-- Pinned rather than "latest" so a newer SDK cannot add analyzer errors to an unchanged tree. -->
    <AnalysisLevel>10.0-recommended</AnalysisLevel>

    <!-- Source-generated configuration binding keeps the trim and AOT declarations true. -->
    <EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator>true</EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator>
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
    <EnableTrimAnalyzer>true</EnableTrimAnalyzer>
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>

    <!-- Dependencies are declared at the minimum versions below, not pinned to the latest patch. -->
    <CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>false</CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\assets\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
      <_Parameter1>HttpResilience.NET.Tests</_Parameter1>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
      <_Parameter1>HttpResilience.NET.IntegrationTests</_Parameter1>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
      <_Parameter1>HttpResilience.NET.Benchmarks</_Parameter1>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="CodeStyle.NET" PrivateAssets="all" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" PrivateAssets="all" />
    <!-- ConfigurationBuilder, for the empty root a code-only registration reads. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Diagnostics" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience" VersionOverride="$(HttpResilienceMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
    <!-- Capped below 9.0.0, which is commercially licensed. Polly.Core is listed too: its types are used here,
         and Polly.Extensions 8.x accepts any Polly.Core at or above its own version, 9.x included. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Polly.Core" VersionOverride="$(PollyVersionRange)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Polly.Extensions" VersionOverride="$(PollyVersionRange)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Polly.RateLimiting" VersionOverride="$(PollyVersionRange)" />
    <!-- Referenced directly: RateLimiterFactory constructs these types, and Polly alone resolves 8.0.0. -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Threading.RateLimiting" VersionOverride="$(ExtensionsMinimumVersion)" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
